    *** AN ARM IS BELOW HALF OF T0's FIRE RATE. Pre-registered as
    UNDERPOWERED rather than null -- a teacher that rarely fires has not
    been tested, and reporting it as a refusal would be the error
    liveness-is-not-dose exists to prevent.
    magnitude: T0 mean|r| 0.0926 vs T1/T2 0.5000 = 5.4x. The PRIMARY contrast
    is magnitude-matched (both T1 arms run the same rule); every comparison
    with T0 is NOT, and T1 is driven HARDER, so a T1 null is not a drive
    shortfall. Baseline memory held at 9.4 trials, alpha 0.00119 (M1c's 0.02
    re-derived for an 17x denser clock).

